schema: encyclopedia-entry
object:
  title: Real Examples of Impact DAOs
  type: encyclopedia-entry
  page_type: case-linked
  summary: >-
    Introduces Impact DAOs (DAOs organized specifically for positive change)
    to a permaculture/regenerative-community audience through three named
    cases — ReFi DAO's global network of place-based Local Nodes, Greenpill's
    "degens to regens" chapter model with tiered participation, and Klima
    DAO's approach to bringing verified carbon credits on-chain — and draws an
    explicit analogy to permaculture principles (working with natural
    systems, local resilience connected to broader networks, sharing over
    hoarding, regenerative over extractive economies).
  audience: permaculture practitioners and regenerative-community members new
    to web3/DAOs
  known_tensions:
    - >-
      Frames DAOs as "trust built into the system rather than relying on one
      person," which risks overstating how automatic trust is in practice —
      DAO participation, accountability, and decision quality are named
      elsewhere in the site as real, unresolved challenges.
    - >-
      Klima DAO's premise (bringing carbon credits on-chain for a liquid,
      accessible market) assumes the underlying off-chain carbon
      verification is sound; the article does not examine that layer's
      integrity.
  related_concepts:
    - impact-dao
  related_resources:
    - refi-dao
    - greenpill-network
    - klima-dao
  maturity: raw
  ai_assisted: true
  provenance:
    origin: src/content/docs/examples-impact-daos.md
    transformation: summarized
    authorship: ai-assisted

